    "issueTitle": "Mirror the GitHub project board on the canvas, with two-way sync",
    "observation": "I want to create a section on the canva that will\nmimic the github project view (The Board style\nview). It should have bidirectional sync. It should\nbe built to have the same sections as the\nconfigured project on github for the workspace\nof the project, like Todo, In Progress, Done, but\nneeds to be dynamic. I dont want to create new\nsections here, but if a new section is created in\ngithub, it should update here. What I want to do\nhere: I want to have a + button on the todo\nsection where it will create a issue block\nautomatically so I can write the issue, it will call\nthe agent, etc (Normal issue block behaviour), I\nwant to be able to move blocks in between\nsections (i will create only on todo!). Let's always\nadd this on the left side of the project canvas\nand we should have a hotkey combination so we\ncan press to move the view to that section. The\nnewest issue should be on top of the list. "
   }
